Changes: ported from Rust to TypeScript and extended with more key and password formats.

The read-only git allowlist used while pausing follows the idea of handoff-now's
freeze allowlist; the code here is written separately.

Ideas taken from other plugins (no code copied; the code here is written separately):
- handoff-now (https://github.com/talal-ai/handoff-now, Apache 2.0): read-only tool
  allowlist while pausing, a handoff written by code when the model cannot, and quoting
  the user's last messages in the handoff.
- agent-usage-guard (https://github.com/rbartoli/agent-usage-guard, MIT, Riccardo Bartoli):
  keeping pause state across reloads, ignoring usage readings whose reset time has passed,
  and letting subagents return while pausing.
- claude-auto-handoff (https://github.com/alexknowshtml/claude-auto-handoff, MIT, Alex Hillman):
  keeping pause state across reloads, listing edited files and the user's last messages,
  and asking whether the last request was finished.
- handoff-guard (https://github.com/angkaworn-dotcom/handoff-guard, MIT): having the resumed
  session confirm the repo state with the user before it starts.
- MohammadMD1383's usage guard (https://github.com/MohammadMD1383): writing a snapshot
  handoff when the turn fails at the limit.
- agent-layer usage-guard: falling back to /usr/bin/git when hooks run without PATH.
- claude-limit-guard: ignoring usage readings whose reset time has passed.
